PROGRAM – 7

TITLE: Configuration Management with Ansible

AIM:
To install and configure Ansible and execute a basic playbook using inventory and modules.

PROCEDURE:

1. Create a user and provide sudo privileges.

   sudo adduser [username]
   sudo usermod -aG sudo username

2. Switch to the user.

   sudo su username

3. Generate SSH key.

   ssh-keygen

4. Copy SSH key to host.

   ssh-copy-id username@localhost
   ssh ansible@localhost

5. Install Ansible.

   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install ansible -y

6. Verify installation.

   ansible --version

7. Create inventory file.

   sudo mkdir -p /etc/ansible
   sudo nano /etc/ansible/hosts

8. Add the following entry:

   [local]
   localhost ansible_connection=local

9. Check inventory.

   ansible-inventory --list -y

10. Test connection.

    ansible all -m ping

COMMANDS:

sudo apt update

sudo apt install ansible -y

ansible --version

ansible all -m ping

OUTPUT:

localhost | SUCCESS

pong

RESULT:
Successfully installed and configured Ansible and tested host connectivity.
